1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,595
The ball flies past you, hits the back
glass, and smacks you in the back.

2
00:00:04,595 --> 00:00:05,263
Point lost.

3
00:00:05,863 --> 00:00:08,487
In padel, the glass is not your enemy.

4
00:00:08,487 --> 00:00:09,698
It's your friend.

5
00:00:09,698 --> 00:00:11,986
And learning that is just level 1.

6
00:00:12,685 --> 00:00:16,320
Today: the five levels of padel,
which one you're really at,

7
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:18,466
and the one skill that moves you up.

8
00:00:18,817 --> 00:00:20,470
First, the numbers.

9
00:00:20,470 --> 00:00:26,668
Playtomic, a booking app a lot of club
players use, rates you from 0 to 7.

10
00:00:26,668 --> 00:00:28,569
Amateurs top out at 5.

11
00:00:28,569 --> 00:00:28,652
6.

12
00:00:29,001 --> 00:00:33,591
It comes from match results: who you played
with, who you played against,

13
00:00:33,591 --> 00:00:35,761
and how sure the app is about you.

14
00:00:35,761 --> 00:00:37,684
So you can win and barely move.

15
00:00:38,034 --> 00:00:41,697
The LTA's padel rating works differently.

16
00:00:41,697 --> 00:00:42,395
From 1.

17
00:00:42,395 --> 00:00:43,093
0 to 7.

18
00:00:43,093 --> 00:00:46,930
0, you pick the sentence that
sounds like you.

19
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:48,586
The numbers differ.

20
00:00:48,586 --> 00:00:49,761
The skills don't.

21
00:00:49,761 --> 00:00:53,808
So my five levels are built on
skills, and the names are mine.

22
00:00:54,158 --> 00:00:56,108
Level 1, the Wall Dodger.

23
00:00:56,108 --> 00:00:57,757
Level 2, the Rallier.

24
00:00:57,757 --> 00:00:59,707
Level 3, the Wall Player.

25
00:00:59,707 --> 00:01:01,582
Level 4, the Net Keeper.

26
00:01:01,582 --> 00:01:04,206
And Level 5, the Tournament Player.

27
00:01:04,706 --> 00:01:06,348
And there's a hidden thread.

28
00:01:06,348 --> 00:01:07,991
Padel is a fight for the net.

29
00:01:08,341 --> 00:01:11,431
In one study of four men's pro finals,

30
00:01:11,431 --> 00:01:16,978
the winning pair played at least one
attacking shot in 85% of points.

31
00:01:16,978 --> 00:01:20,544
The losing pair played none
in 47% of points.

32
00:01:21,444 --> 00:01:25,583
Every level up gives you one more tool
to win the net, or keep it.

33
00:01:25,933 --> 00:01:27,820
On the LTA scale, the 1.

34
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:31,821
0 player is still working on
getting the ball in play.

35
00:01:32,171 --> 00:01:36,568
Rule one: your shot must land on the
floor of the other side first.

36
00:01:36,568 --> 00:01:40,512
If it hits their glass before it
bounces, you lose the point.

37
00:01:40,862 --> 00:01:44,336
Rule two: after one bounce, the
ball can hit any wall,

38
00:01:44,336 --> 00:01:47,241
and it's still in play until
it bounces again.

39
00:01:47,591 --> 00:01:49,186
The serve is underarm.

40
00:01:49,186 --> 00:01:54,524
Bounce the ball, then hit it at or below your
waist, diagonally into the box.

41
00:01:54,874 --> 00:01:57,732
Think of a wall passing the
ball back to you.

42
00:01:57,732 --> 00:02:00,527
Wait, and it comes to you,
slower and easier.

43
00:02:00,877 --> 00:02:06,313
Before any drill in this video, warm up for
6 to 8 minutes: easy jogging,

44
00:02:06,313 --> 00:02:11,014
side shuffles, leg swings, lunges,
calf raises and arm circles.

45
00:02:11,014 --> 00:02:14,466
Then volleys and
groundstrokes, overheads last.

46
00:02:14,817 --> 00:02:17,192
New to padel, or back after a break?

47
00:02:17,192 --> 00:02:21,494
Build up your court time week by week,
and don't play through pain.

48
00:02:21,844 --> 00:02:23,890
To move up, read the back glass.

49
00:02:23,890 --> 00:02:27,611
Prepare your racket early, let the
ball come off the glass,

50
00:02:27,611 --> 00:02:29,161
and take the pace off it.

51
00:02:29,511 --> 00:02:31,254
The drill: toss and turn.

52
00:02:31,254 --> 00:02:36,013
Your partner tosses a ball that bounces
once and hits your back glass.

53
00:02:36,013 --> 00:02:38,962
Turn side-on, let it come
off, and catch it.

54
00:02:39,312 --> 00:02:41,309
3 sets of 10, twice a week.

55
00:02:41,309 --> 00:02:43,877
Then swap the catch for a soft shot.

56
00:02:44,777 --> 00:02:45,556
The mistake?

57
00:02:45,556 --> 00:02:47,414
Swinging like a tennis player.

58
00:02:47,414 --> 00:02:49,812
Keep your backswing short on both sides.

59
00:02:50,412 --> 00:02:51,298
The LTA 2.

60
00:02:51,298 --> 00:02:55,809
5 player can rally with basic
shots, but lacks technique.

61
00:02:56,159 --> 00:02:59,678
The Rallier trap: one partner at
the net, one at the back.

62
00:02:59,678 --> 00:03:02,004
The ball goes straight through the gap.

63
00:03:02,355 --> 00:03:07,518
The LTA's two normal shapes: both up at
the net, or both back defending.

64
00:03:07,867 --> 00:03:10,843
Think of two windscreen
wipers tied together.

65
00:03:10,843 --> 00:03:11,878
You move as one.

66
00:03:12,228 --> 00:03:15,151
To move up: be consistent,
and move as a pair.

67
00:03:15,501 --> 00:03:17,772
Drill 1: the cross-court count.

68
00:03:17,772 --> 00:03:22,456
Rally diagonally in half the court and
count your longest streak.

69
00:03:22,456 --> 00:03:24,088
3 rounds of 3 minutes.

70
00:03:24,088 --> 00:03:26,146
Aim for 10 in a row, then 20.

71
00:03:26,496 --> 00:03:28,446
Drill 2: mirror shadowing.

72
00:03:28,446 --> 00:03:29,095
No ball.

73
00:03:29,095 --> 00:03:33,283
A coach calls "up" or "back", and
you both move together.

74
00:03:33,283 --> 00:03:34,944
4 rounds of 30 seconds.

75
00:03:35,294 --> 00:03:40,201
Call "mine" or "yours" on balls down the
middle, so you don't clash rackets.

76
00:03:40,551 --> 00:03:41,352
The mistake?

77
00:03:41,352 --> 00:03:43,261
Hitting hard to win the point.

78
00:03:43,261 --> 00:03:44,924
Placement beats power here.

79
00:03:45,524 --> 00:03:46,313
At LTA 3.

80
00:03:46,313 --> 00:03:52,073
0, you're pretty consistent and can use
tactics like playing off the wall.

81
00:03:52,423 --> 00:03:53,123
The problem?

82
00:03:53,123 --> 00:03:56,946
You're stuck at the back, defending, while
the other pair owns the net.

83
00:03:57,296 --> 00:03:58,983
The way out is the lob.

84
00:03:58,983 --> 00:04:02,569
The LTA calls it the most
important shot in padel.

85
00:04:02,569 --> 00:04:06,576
It pushes the net pair back and
buys you time to move in.

86
00:04:06,926 --> 00:04:09,306
Picture a rainbow over a castle wall.

87
00:04:09,306 --> 00:04:12,814
You can't go through the
defenders, so you go over them.

88
00:04:13,164 --> 00:04:18,307
Hit it high, cross-court, landing just past
the service line and before the back

89
00:04:18,307 --> 00:04:18,751
glass.

90
00:04:18,751 --> 00:04:21,100
Bend your legs and swing low to high.

91
00:04:21,450 --> 00:04:23,347
The drill: two up, two back.

92
00:04:23,347 --> 00:04:28,713
The pair at the back starts every point with a
lob, then the point is played out.

93
00:04:28,713 --> 00:04:30,087
Swap every 2 points.

94
00:04:30,087 --> 00:04:31,199
First pair to 10.

95
00:04:31,549 --> 00:04:36,221
If you're being lobbed, turn side-on and run
back, but stop short of the glass.

96
00:04:36,571 --> 00:04:40,104
Let the lob bounce and come off
the wall, then play it.

97
00:04:40,104 --> 00:04:42,502
One player chases, the other calls it.

98
00:04:42,852 --> 00:04:43,657
The mistake?

99
00:04:43,657 --> 00:04:46,567
Hitting a great lob, then
staying at the back.

100
00:04:46,567 --> 00:04:48,734
The lob is your ticket to the net.

101
00:04:48,734 --> 00:04:49,167
Use it.

102
00:04:49,867 --> 00:04:50,626
At LTA 4.

103
00:04:50,626 --> 00:04:56,694
0, you're controlled, you cover the court well,
and you know basic padel tactics.

104
00:04:57,043 --> 00:05:00,312
Now you hold the net, so the
other pair lobs you.

105
00:05:00,312 --> 00:05:02,078
Your answer is the bandeja.

106
00:05:02,428 --> 00:05:04,598
Bandeja is Spanish for "tray".

107
00:05:04,598 --> 00:05:10,127
It's an overhead with an open face, hit at
about eye height, across your body,

108
00:05:10,127 --> 00:05:10,897
with slice.

109
00:05:11,247 --> 00:05:13,162
It's not meant to win the point.

110
00:05:13,162 --> 00:05:14,554
It keeps you at the net.

111
00:05:15,154 --> 00:05:17,526
Think of carrying a tray of drinks.

112
00:05:17,526 --> 00:05:19,899
Smooth and flat, so nothing spills.

113
00:05:19,899 --> 00:05:21,810
A smash is throwing the tray.

114
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:28,298
In those pro finals, bandejas were
about 23% of attacking shots.

115
00:05:28,298 --> 00:05:30,565
Smashes, only about 12%.

116
00:05:30,915 --> 00:05:33,254
Its attacking cousin is the víbora,

117
00:05:33,254 --> 00:05:38,126
or "viper": an overhead hit around head or
shoulder height, with side-spin.

118
00:05:38,476 --> 00:05:40,351
Drill 1: shadow bandeja.

119
00:05:40,351 --> 00:05:41,026
No ball.

120
00:05:41,026 --> 00:05:46,727
Turn sideways, racket up like a tray, swing
across your body at eye height,

121
00:05:46,727 --> 00:05:48,978
then step back in to the net.

122
00:05:48,978 --> 00:05:49,953
3 sets of 10.

123
00:05:50,303 --> 00:05:52,059
Drill 2: defend the net.

124
00:05:52,059 --> 00:05:54,096
2 at the net, 2 at the back.

125
00:05:54,096 --> 00:05:55,501
The back pair lobs.

126
00:05:55,501 --> 00:06:00,628
The net pair must land a bandeja past the
service line, then play it out.

127
00:06:00,979 --> 00:06:02,547
Swap every 2 points.

128
00:06:02,547 --> 00:06:03,518
First to 10.

129
00:06:03,518 --> 00:06:09,491
Start with soft hand-fed lobs, and go live
once most of your bandejas land deep.

130
00:06:09,841 --> 00:06:15,175
Before you start, careful: the typical padel
calf tear happens when you land on one

131
00:06:15,175 --> 00:06:18,033
leg after an overhead and
push off to volley.

132
00:06:18,383 --> 00:06:22,876
So first, build your calves: calf
raises 2 or 3 times a week,

133
00:06:22,876 --> 00:06:27,876
straight-knee and bent-knee, 3 sets of 10
to 15, building to one leg.

134
00:06:28,226 --> 00:06:31,610
Keep early overhead sessions to
about 10 minutes,

135
00:06:31,610 --> 00:06:34,046
and land on both feet when you can.

136
00:06:34,046 --> 00:06:38,039
If your shoulder or calf already
hurts, see a physio first.

137
00:06:38,389 --> 00:06:39,281
The mistake?

138
00:06:39,281 --> 00:06:40,654
Smashing every lob.

139
00:06:40,654 --> 00:06:42,988
Then backing off to the baseline.

140
00:06:42,988 --> 00:06:45,322
Hit the bandeja, and step back in.

141
00:06:46,023 --> 00:06:46,604
LTA 5.

142
00:06:46,604 --> 00:06:53,079
0 is an experienced tournament player with a
very good understanding of padel

143
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:53,660
tactics.

144
00:06:54,010 --> 00:06:55,623
The jump isn't a new shot.

145
00:06:55,623 --> 00:06:58,191
It's choosing the right one
under pressure.

146
00:06:58,541 --> 00:07:04,606
The por tres, or x3: a kick smash from close to
the net that bounces out over the

147
00:07:04,606 --> 00:07:05,346
side wall.

148
00:07:05,697 --> 00:07:07,047
And the big points.

149
00:07:07,047 --> 00:07:11,500
With golden point scoring, deuce is
settled by one deciding point.

150
00:07:11,849 --> 00:07:17,396
In men's pro golden points, more than 60%
ended in an error, not a winner.

151
00:07:17,746 --> 00:07:19,724
Drill 1: golden-point sets.

152
00:07:19,724 --> 00:07:24,175
Play every deuce as one deciding
point, and count your errors.

153
00:07:24,175 --> 00:07:25,447
1 set per session.

154
00:07:25,797 --> 00:07:27,620
Drill 2: attack or reset.

155
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:33,440
The net pair may only smash short lobs they can
hit without stepping back past the

156
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:34,352
service line.

157
00:07:34,702 --> 00:07:39,304
Anything that pushes them back must
be a bandeja or a víbora.

158
00:07:39,304 --> 00:07:40,121
Play to 10.

159
00:07:40,471 --> 00:07:44,995
Strength train all your major muscle
groups at least 2 days a week.

160
00:07:44,995 --> 00:07:50,583
Start light, build up gradually, and if
something already hurts, see a physio first.

161
00:07:50,933 --> 00:07:56,524
In a review of sports trials, strength training
cut injury rates to about a third of

162
00:07:56,524 --> 00:07:59,418
normal, and balance training
to about half.

163
00:07:59,418 --> 00:08:00,997
Stretching didn't help.

164
00:08:00,997 --> 00:08:05,141
Only a few trials tested strength
work, and none were in padel.

165
00:08:05,491 --> 00:08:06,287
The mistake?

166
00:08:06,287 --> 00:08:08,674
Going for a winner on every high ball.

167
00:08:08,674 --> 00:08:09,715
Pick your moment.

168
00:08:10,415 --> 00:08:15,940
In a review of padel injury studies, the elbow
was the most commonly injured spot.

169
00:08:16,290 --> 00:08:21,773
Tennis elbow alone made up more than 20%
of injuries in another review.

170
00:08:22,123 --> 00:08:25,305
Pick a racket weight and grip
size that suit you.

171
00:08:25,305 --> 00:08:29,696
If your outer elbow still hurts after a
few days' rest, see a doctor.

172
00:08:30,046 --> 00:08:34,757
The ball is small and fast, and
experience doesn't protect your eyes.

173
00:08:34,757 --> 00:08:39,603
Sports goggles with polycarbonate lenses
are worth wearing at any level.

174
00:08:39,953 --> 00:08:43,494
And at the net, don't turn round to
watch your partner's shot.

175
00:08:43,845 --> 00:08:48,860
Stop and get checked if you feel a sudden pop
or snap at the back of your calf or

176
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:51,184
heel, or can't push up onto your toes.

177
00:08:51,533 --> 00:08:56,371
If the ball hits you in the eye, stop playing
and get it checked by a doctor the

178
00:08:56,371 --> 00:08:56,909
same day.

179
00:08:57,259 --> 00:09:02,395
Go to the emergency room straight away if
your vision changes, light hurts,

180
00:09:02,395 --> 00:09:05,707
you feel sick, or you can't
open or move the eye.

181
00:09:06,057 --> 00:09:07,364
So which are you?

182
00:09:07,364 --> 00:09:08,743
Dodging the glass?

183
00:09:08,743 --> 00:09:09,396
Level 1.

184
00:09:09,396 --> 00:09:11,211
Split from your partner?

185
00:09:11,211 --> 00:09:11,864
Level 2.

186
00:09:11,864 --> 00:09:13,243
Stuck at the back?

187
00:09:13,243 --> 00:09:13,896
Level 3.

188
00:09:13,896 --> 00:09:15,348
Smashing every lob?

189
00:09:15,348 --> 00:09:16,001
Level 4.

190
00:09:16,001 --> 00:09:17,380
Losing big points?

191
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:17,961
Level 5.

192
00:09:18,461 --> 00:09:22,408
This week: warm up, then do the
drills for your level, twice.

193
00:09:22,758 --> 00:09:27,413
Next time the ball flies past you into
the back glass, don't flinch.

194
00:09:27,413 --> 00:09:30,246
Turn, wait, and let the wall pass it back.
